 - CLI parsing accommodates further evaluation subcommands (e.g., `frai eval bias`).
 
+## Threshold Feature (Added Later)
+- Allows CLI and SDK users to set minimum score requirements for metrics.
+- Syntax: `--threshold <metric>=<min>` (can be specified multiple times).
+- Thresholds must be numeric between 0 and 1; invalid thresholds exit with code 2.
+- Reports include `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` array with per-metric results.
+- Markdown reports include a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL status.
+- Exit code 0 if all thresholds pass, 1 if any fail, 2 for malformed input.
+- Metrics with null scores automatically fail their thresholds (safety default).
+- Works seamlessly with custom metrics via SDK.
+
 ## Follow-up Tasks
 1. Integrate real toxicity/bias models once provider abstraction is implemented (Phase 0 → Providers milestone).
 2. Extend datasets loader to support configurable schema mapping.
